 0.4em 0 0.5em;\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Star1\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"9\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Star1_fd1ea6.png\" width=\"10\"/></span><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Star1\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"9\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Star1_fd1ea6.png\" width=\"10\"/></span></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Maps and Pictures</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"map\">\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Brain Grounds -1\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"77\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Brain_Grounds_1_d47691.png\" width=\"125\"/></span> <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Brain Grounds -2\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"80\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Brain_Grounds_2_e4104b.png\" width=\"125\"/></span> <span typeof=\"mw:File\"><img alt=\"Brain Grounds -3\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"86\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Brain_Grounds_3_b1e374.png\" width=\"125\"/></span> </div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Other Properties</h2>\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"implemented\">\n<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version</h3>\n<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><span class=\"implementation-date\">12.30.9287<br/>December 02, 2019<br/>Winter Update 2019</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><p>\t    See also: Hunting Places <span class=\"explained\">Help</span></p></nav>\n</aside>\n<p><br/>\nThe <b>Brain Grounds</b> consist of an organic environment which seems to be controlled by a central Brain. It can be accessed through an invisible teleport north of the <a href=\"#/wiki/Jakundaf%20Desert\">Jakundaf Desert</a>. It is a popular hunting spawn due to the big amount of creatures that can be lured into the bigger rooms at the same time and the fact that it can be hunted in several different party combinations or just solo.\n</p><p>There are three floors with increasing difficulty, and a <a class=\"coord-link\" data-coord=\"31904,32347,9\" title=\"Ver no mapa\">portal (31904, 32347, 9)</a> on the second floor that brings players to the <a href=\"#/wiki/Netherworld\">Netherworld</a>, which is sometimes used as part of the hunting area if the player or party hunting is too strong for the Brain Grounds alone.\n</p><p>Access to this area is obtained as part of the <a href=\"#/quest/feaster-of-souls-quest\">Feaster of Souls Quest</a>.\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-First_Floor\">First Floor</span></h2>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div><table cellspacing=\"0\" class=\"wikitable sortable full-width\"><tbody><tr><th>Name</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"width: 38px; text-align: center;\">Exp</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">HP</th><th data-sort-type=\"number\" style=\"text-align: center;\">Max. Damage</th><th style=\"font-size: small;\">Loot</th></tr>\n<tr><td style=\"width: 100px; text-align: center\"><span class=\"no-pseudoelements-container\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"#/wiki/Grim%20Reaper\"><img alt=\"Grim Reaper\" class=\"mw-file-element\" height=\"64\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Grim_Reaper_c19784.gif\" width=\"64\"/></a></span></span><br/><a href=\"#/wiki/Grim%20Reaper\">Grim Reaper</a></td><td style=\"width: 38px; text-align: center;\">5,500</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">3,900</td><td style=\"text-align: center;\">2595 (<span style=\"white-space: nowrap\">1600 <span class=\"icon\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeo